# Jw_cad itself is Jiro Shimizu & Yoshifumi Tanaka's.  Its licence allows
# passing it on, on two conditions: do not change the program, and pass it on
# in the form it came in (Jw_win.txt, section 3).  So the installer is here
# exactly as it is downloaded -- jww10036.exe, an unmodified Inno Setup
# package -- and the expanded tree is not: orig/ is what the installer makes
# locally.  README.md says how to make it.
orig/
install.log

# The decompilation itself is in the repository (2026-09-28): decomp/byclass,
# decomp/decomp, decomp/rtti and decomp/inventory.csv are Ghidra's output for
# Jw_win.exe, which is what every line of src/ was written from, so the
# working can be followed without a Ghidra run of your own.
#
# decomp/res is **not**: that is the original's own data taken straight out of
# it -- its bitmaps, icons, menus and strings -- together with the .jww files
# the original itself draws for the tests to be scored against.  Those are
# made locally by tools/gen.sh from your own copy of the installer.
decomp/res/

tmp/
__pycache__/
*.o
tests/*.exe

# generated from your own copy of Jw_win.exe by tools/mkres.py and
# tools/btnmap.py -- machine output from someone else's program
src/gen/
tests/out/
jw_port.exe
sync.tgz
